<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argonauts</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Argonauts were the band of heroes in Greek mythology who sailed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jason">Jason</a> on the ship <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argo</a> to Colchis, on the eastern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, to fetch the Golden Fleece. With the help of the Colchian princess Medea they took the fleece from King Aeetes. The story, told most fully in the Argonautica of Apollonius of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a>, shaped Greek ideas of Colchis as a land of gold.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argonauts.jpg" alt="Argonauts" width="330" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Niobid Painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krater_Niobid_Painter_A_Louvre_G341.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…the Greeks Colchis was Aea, from the 5th century BCE onwards the home of Aeëtes, Medea and the Golden Fleece, the goal of Jason and the <b>Argonauts</b>; here Prometheus was chained to a mountain for revealing fire to humanity, and here some placed the homeland of the Amazons.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-colchis">Kingdom of Colchis · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
